{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916011-between-serial-killers-and-slashers","id":916011,"title":"Between Serial Killers and Slashers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-16T20:50:48-07:00","id":916011,"title":"Between Serial Killers and Slashers","content":"Okay, so we all agree that slashers are fun to use once in a session. But where do you guys consider the line to be between a &quot;typical&quot; serial killers that we're used to, and the slasher killers that CofD introduced?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T07:34:58-07:00","id":916186,"title":"","content":"To me it comes down to what you want them to be able to do. If they're &quot;mundane&quot; serial killers, then I use the Ripper level Undertakings. They get a mechanical boost but are overall still pretty grounded. If you want them to be able to do things that are explicitly supernatural, then you've crossed into Scourge territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T07:38:14-07:00","id":916189,"title":"","content":"Yeah. If you're actually using a serial killer, as in a mundane mortal who has an uncontrollable urge to kill people, you should just use a ripper. They don't have to all be a super-competent one but that's what the ripper type is there for.<br /> <br /> If you want someone who has killed people but isn't a serial killer, for instance many mortal characters at the end of a chronicle or most action heroes, then you're just dealing with a mortal who's taken some Integrity Breaking Points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T07:40:12-07:00","id":916190,"title":"","content":"If the serial killer is worth his own horror movie, he's a Slasher. If he's worth his own horror franchise, he's a Scourge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T07:45:28-07:00","id":916193,"title":"","content":"For 2e, I suggested a Tier setup for this:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Tier One: Serial Killer<br /> \u2022 Tier Two: Ripper<br /> \u2022 Tier Three: Scourge","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T09:35:07-07:00","id":916273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916011-between-serial-killers-and-slashers?p=916190#post916190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the serial killer is worth his own horror movie, he's a Slasher. If he's worth his own horror franchise, he's a Scourge.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pretty much this! In my mind there is a bit of a difference in serial killers and Slashers though. I feel like a serial killer is, pardon the term for such a monster, but more mundane than a Slasher. Typically a mortal with mental disorders and terrible compulsions. I think crossing over to a Slasher represents on the Ripper level a touch of the supernatural, and on the Scourge level a slathering of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11942-the13thghost","name":"The13thGhost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T10:19:57-07:00","id":916300,"title":"","content":"The book is pretty clear that rippers are not magical at all, this is represented by their Talent, which is 'abnormal, eerie, even awe-inspiring, but they aren't magical.' And their Frailty, which 'logical extensions of their madness and shortcomings, not arcane secrets that hunters can use to bring them down.'<br /> <br /> If you don't want to use rippers for 'mundane' serial killers, that's fine, but that is what they are for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T10:45:48-07:00","id":916320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916011-between-serial-killers-and-slashers?p=916300#post916300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book is pretty clear that rippers are not magical at all, this is represented by their Talent, which is 'abnormal, eerie, even awe-inspiring, but they aren't magical.' And their Frailty, which 'logical extensions of their madness and shortcomings, not arcane secrets that hunters can use to bring them down.'<br /> <br /> If you don't want to use rippers for 'mundane' serial killers, that's fine, but that is what they are for.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> After going back and checking out the wikia and the book, I have to say you are right. I guess my mind sort of transposed some of the sections of VASCU's write up where it says they define Slashers as being supernatural killers as the baseline.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11942-the13thghost","name":"The13thGhost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T10:45:53-07:00","id":916321,"title":"","content":"Rippers are for exceptional serial killers. Ordinary serial killers (the equivalent of tier one) shouldn't have an Undertaking at all. Yes, there's a divide between Ripper and Scourge, and rippers are on the \u201cnot supernatural\u201d side of that divide; but that doesn't mean that everything on that side is a ripper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}